⟦ write_hook_autofix | PROPOSAL-v1 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-09-09T16:38:05Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status proposed

// PROBLEM: hand-written VSM signatures fail validation (wrong version,
// hardcoded timestamps incl. the :00-seconds trap, header/footer mismatch).
// Parametric generation (vsm_kernel.new_doc) fixes creation; existing and
// pasted documents still hit the write gate as BLOCKED with no repair path.
//
// PROPOSAL (design only — write_gates.vsm NOT modified by this doc):
// A normalize-only fixer gate for .vsm writes. Allowed repairs:
//   1. version -> vsm-1.2.1 / @vsm 1.2.1
//   2. timestamp -> fresh get_timestamp() (never hardcoded shapes)
//   3. footer -> short form ⟦ /name ⟧ with header name match
// FORBIDDEN: touching any body line, changing @status, inventing content.
// Flow: gate runs fixer in dry-run -> prints unified diff as advisory ->
//   (phase 2, needs S5) blocking mode applies fix ONLY if diff touches
//   signature lines exclusively; otherwise stays BLOCKED.
// ROLLOUT: register as advisory gate first, measure 2 sessions, then S5
// decides blocking. A0/A5/R17/R4 unaffected. Techo de autonomia intacto.
//
// S5 DECISION REQUIRED: approve advisory registration / approve blocking.
⟦ /write_hook_autofix ⟧
